   "speaker": "TechLead",
   "act": "state",
   "content": [
    "The System must ensure that audit trail data is available for inspection on request, so that a specific event can be identified and all related data made accessible, and that this can be achieved by authorised external personnel who have little or no familiarity with the system."
   ]
  },
  {
   "speaker": "Client",
   "act": "state",
   "content": [
    "The System must be able to export audit trails for specified cases (without affecting the audit trail stored by the System). This functionality can be used by external auditors who wish to examine or analyse system activity.",
    "The System must at a minimum be able to provide reports for actions on cases organised: By case; By user; In chronological sequence."
   ]
  }
 ],
 "turns": [
  {
   "id": "M1:T21",
   "speaker": "Analyst",
   "act": "echo",
   "guide": "Analyst paraphrases the content back as a question, to confirm understanding.",
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "The System must at a minimum be able to provide reports for actions on cases organised: By case; By user; In chronological sequence.",
     "role": "echo"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T22",
   "speaker": "Client",
   "act": "confirm",
   "guide": "Short confirmation that the paraphrase is right."
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T23",
   "speaker": "Analyst",
   "act": "anything_else",
   "guide": "Analyst asks whether there is anything else on 'audit module'."
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T24",
   "speaker": "Client",
   "act": "nothing_else",
   "guide": "Short answer: nothing else on this topic."
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T25",
   "speaker": "Analyst",
   "act": "ask_topic",
   "guide": "Analyst moves the discussion to the topic 'access module' and asks about it."
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T26",
   "speaker": "TechLead",
   "act": "state",
   "guide": "The speaker states the content in their own words.",
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "The System must allow changes to security attributes for groups or users (such as access rights, security level, privileges, password allocation and management) to be made only by super-user.",
     "role": "statement"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T27",
   "speaker": "Client",
   "act": "state",
   "guide": "The speaker states the content in their own words.",
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "If a user requests access to, or searches for, a case which he does not have the right to access, the System must provide one of the following responses (selectable at configuration time): display title and metadata; display the existence of a case but not its title or other metadata; do not display any case information or indicate its existence in any way. These options are presented in order of increasing security. Note that the requirement in the third option (i.e. the most stringent) implies that the System must not include such cases in any count of search results; this level of security is normally appropriate for cases dealing with matters such as national security.",
     "role": "statement"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T28",
   "speaker": "TechLead",
   "act": "state",
   "guide": "The speaker states the content in their own words.",
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "If a user performs a quick or advanced search, the System must never include in the search result list any record which the user does not have the right to access.",
     "role": "statement"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T29",
   "speaker": "Analyst",
   "act": "anything_else",
   "guide": "Analyst asks whether there is anything else on 'access module'."
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T30",
   "speaker": "Client",
   "act": "nothing_else",
   "guide": "Short answer: nothing else on this topic."
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T31",
   "speaker": "Analyst",
   "act": "ask_topic",
   "guide": "Analyst moves the discussion to the topic 'ease of use' and asks about it."
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T32",
   "speaker": "TechLead",
   "act": "state",
   "guide": "The speaker states the content in their own words.",
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "All error messages produced by the System must be meaningful, so that they can be appropriately acted upon by the users who are likely to see them. Ideally, each error message will be accompanied by explanatory text and an indication of the action(s) which the user can take in response to the error.",
     "role": "statement"
    },
    {
     "text": "The System must provide End User and Administrator functions which are easy to use and intuitive throughout.",
     "role": "statement"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T33",
   "speaker": "Analyst",
   "act": "anything_else",
   "guide": "Analyst asks whether there is anything else on 'ease of use'."
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T34",
   "speaker": "TechLead",
   "act": "nothing_else",
   "guide": "Short answer: nothing else on this topic."
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T35",
   "speaker": "Analyst",
   "act": "ask_topic",
   "guide": "Analyst moves the discussion to the topic 'usability' and asks about it."
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T36",
   "speaker": "Client",
   "act": "state",
   "guide": "The speaker states the content in their own words.",
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "The user interfaces should be designed to make them user-intuitive.",
     "role": "statement"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T37",
   "speaker": "Analyst",
   "act": "backchannel",
   "guide": "Short acknowledgment while listening (1-3 words)."
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T38",
   "speaker": "TechLead",
   "act": "state",
   "guide": "The speaker states the content in their own words.",
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "The user interfaces of the system should comply with Standard ISO 9241.",
     "role": "statement"
    },
    {
     "text": "Providing text equivalents for non-text media objects: All non-text media objects, such as graphical images or video, should be provided with alternative equivalent textual descriptions and/or with equivalent text-based functionality.",
     "role": "statement"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T39",
   "speaker": "Client",
   "act": "state",
   "guide": "The speaker states the content in their own words.",
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Making navigation self-descriptive: Navigation should be designed to help users understand where they are, where they have been and where they can go next. General guidance on achieving self-descriptiveness is given in ISO 9241-110.",
     "role": "statement"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
